ne prescriptions and detect omissions and/or errors before they become a customer service problem; and Medication Spend Analyzer to break down the monthly drug spending for each of the LTCFs. Guardian Pharmacy Services, Inc. was founded in 2003 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Fred P. Burke | CEO, President & Director | Age 75 | Compensation: $845,842 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $402K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $24K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Guardian Pharmacy Services, Inc is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $3.1B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 35% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 26-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 20% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $87M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.04\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.9% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 45% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented 